From 474aaa78152c582f989c1f93195b461fc76b968a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:17:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] fix(admin): typed confirmation and audit for
 irreversible deletes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bug: "clear all API logs" and "delete all media" were one unauthenticated-
by-phrase API call away for anyone with the menu's write permission; the
three-step dialogs lived only in the browser. Deleting a connection, an
Alpharouter API key or a personal key left no trace at all, and the per-
resource changelog tables cascade away with the resource, so nothing could
be reconstructed afterwards.

Change:
- DELETE /api/admin/logs and POST /api/admin/storage/clear-cache now need
  Super Admin (on top of the menu write permission) and a body
  {"confirm": "DELETE ALL LOGS" | "DELETE ALL MEDIA"}; wrong phrase -> 400.
  A security_audit_events row with the row count (logs) or asset count and
  total bytes (media) is written *before* the delete.
- log_connection_deleted / log_api_key_deleted write to
  security_audit_events (no FK to the resource, so it survives) with a
  snapshot that excludes the API key / key hash; admin and self-service
  personal key deletion write user_api_key_deleted.
- UI: the third dialog step in ApiLogs and StorageManagement is now a typed
  prompt and the phrase is posted to the server.

Tests: tests/test_destructive_admin_ops.py — wrong/missing phrase leaves
data intact and writes no audit; correct phrase deletes and audits counts;
connection/key/personal-key deletions leave audit rows without secrets;
cross-user personal key deletion still 404.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
